Accept a WebTransport connection at 0.5-RTT (wtransport 0.7.2).

A quinn server connection may send as soon as its handshake flight is out,
but wtransport waits for the whole handshake before its driver sends the
HTTP/3 SETTINGS, and Chromium sends the CONNECT only once SETTINGS arrive:
a cold session cost three round trips. With SETTINGS at 0.5-RTT it costs
two (Chromium at a 47 ms RTT: `ready` 145 ms -> 97 ms). The release build
applies this to the vendored crate; development runs unpatched, where the
round trip is zero anyway.

--- a/src/endpoint.rs
+++ b/src/endpoint.rs
@@ -613,7 +613,13 @@

     fn new(quic_incoming: quinn::Incoming) -> Self {
         Self(Box::pin(async move {
-            let quic_connection = quic_incoming.await?;
+            // Server side, into_0rtt always succeeds: the connection is usable
+            // for 0.5-RTT data, so SETTINGS leave with the server's handshake
+            // flight instead of a round trip later.
+            let quic_connection = match quic_incoming.accept()?.into_0rtt() {
+                Ok((connection, _)) => connection,
+                Err(connecting) => connecting.await?,
+            };
             Self::accept(quic_connection).await
         }))
     }
